### GAME (Generative Adaptive MIDI Extractor)
- Upstream: Team OpenVPI, https://github.com/openvpi/GAME
- License: MIT (code) / Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International
  (the released models, namioto/models/LICENSE-CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0.txt) — the models are NOT AGPL-3.0
- Used for: extracting notes from a singing voice. `namioto/game.py` is a port of the standalone
  `infer_onnx.py` that goes with GAME's ONNX model exports - GAME itself is a PyTorch project and
  ships no ONNX inference - so the module keeps GAME's MIT license, while the models stay a separate
  work under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. The models are not redistributed here: `namioto-game` downloads the
  size that was asked for (small 46 MB / medium 180 MB / large 362 MB) from GAME's GitHub release
  into the data directory - `platformdirs.user_data_dir("namioto")/models/game/<size>`, so
  ~/.local/share/namioto/models/game/small on Linux - and a directory of them can also be given
  directly with `--model` or `$NAMIOTO_GAME_MODEL`.
- Consequence: a transcription produced with those models is non-commercial, exactly as with the
  bundled TempoCNN model above.

### FA-Kara (forced alignment)
- Upstream: moriwx/FA-Kara, https://github.com/moriwx/FA-Kara
- License: MIT
- Used for: the alignment core `namioto/align.py` ports. `align()`'s per-token flow - flatten a
  line's tokens into characters, force them onto the model's frames, group the frames back into one
  span per token - is reimplemented here in numpy and ONNX Runtime, with the audio windowed by the
  caller. The model is not redistributed: the module loads a converted ONNX graph from the data
  directory (`~/.local/share/namioto/models/<model>/<language>`, via `platformdirs`) or from
  `$NAMIOTO_ALIGN_MODEL`, and `scripts/export_align_model.py` produces it from the two models below.

### torchaudio (CTC forced alignment)
- Upstream: pytorch/audio, https://github.com/pytorch/audio
- License: BSD 2-Clause
- Used for: `forced_align` and `merge_tokens`, whose numpy port in `namioto/align.py` computes the
  CTC trellis and the token spans. torchaudio is not a dependency of the program; only
  `scripts/export_align_model.py` uses it, to convert the MMS checkpoint.

### MMS forced-alignment model (not redistributed)
- Upstream: Meta AI, `torchaudio.pipelines.MMS_FA` (the `ctc_alignment_mling_uroman` checkpoint)
- License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International — NOT AGPL-3.0
- Namioto's default aligner (`--model mms`); `scripts/export_align_model.py` converts it from the
  network, and it is never shipped with the program.

### yohane karaoke alignment model (not redistributed)
- Upstream: `NextFire/mms-300m-ForcedAligner-karaoke-ja-Latn`,
  https://huggingface.co/NextFire/mms-300m-ForcedAligner-karaoke-ja-Latn
- License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International — NOT AGPL-3.0
- Namioto's `--model yohane`; `scripts/export_align_model.py` converts it from HuggingFace, and it is
  never shipped with the program.
- Consequence: a converted aligner is non-commercial, like the bundled TempoCNN and GAME's models.

